A game backend

The group `Game` holds `Matchmaker` and `Game server`. `Player` calls the
`Matchmaker`, with the label `ask`. The `Matchmaker` sends to a `Game server`,
with the label `assign`. The `Game server` writes to `Stats`, with the label
`results`, as `server/results.go` line 30 shows. The `Player` must never call
`Stats` directly. Show it as a flow.
---
Game { Matchmaker, Game server }
Player -> Matchmaker: ask
Matchmaker -> Game server: assign
Game server -> Stats: results @ server/results.go:30
Player -x Stats
show flow
